    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "515141",
        "date_added": "2026-10-25 09:01:16",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static delivery-chain correlation, 2026-10-25 UTC. Verified SHA-256; complete 100,540-byte ELF32 little-endian ARM. It contains the exact HTTP delivery URL http://94.154.43.192/bins/kla.sh. At 08:58:51 UTC, bounded read-only retrieval of that file URL returned HTTP 200 and an 8,338-byte shell loader, SHA-256 33df26a65740c720c1d8f5c74b1372089a73df6288cc75e198e89d68aa606826. Isolated inspection of the retrieved script confirms architecture selection, wget/curl and BusyBox fallback paths, use of a robben output name, permission changes, launch with the configured IPHOST argument, and process termination for named competitors. The script sets its CNC/IPHOST variables to the delivery host, but variable names do not independently establish a C2 protocol or control port. This verifies the current script delivery and correlates it with an embedded literal in this ELF; it is not a claim that this binary executed or downloaded that file. Architecture payloads were not executed or fetched in this batch. Other IP literals, common DNS resolvers and browser version strings were not promoted to C2 IOCs."
      }
    ],
